blocks.en:
We discard samples that would compromise downstream evaluation through four criteria:
(i) images with zero or multiple detected faces, which introduce annotation ambiguity;
(ii) non-RGB images ( e.g. , grayscale, infrared), which are incompatible with color-dependent estimators, in particular rPPG;
(iii) heavily blurred images, particularly prevalent in WebFace42M;
(iv) cross-dataset duplicate identities, identified by computing pairwise cosine similarities between per-identity mean embeddings from
a pretrained ArcFace model Deng et al. (2019) from the InsightFace library.
Identity pairs whose cosine similarity exceeds τ id = 0.55 \tau_{\text{id}}=0.55 are merged (when from different sources) or the lower-quality instance removed. The threshold τ id = 0.55 \tau_{\text{id}}=0.55 was chosen empirically: on a held-out set of manually verified same-identity and different-identity pairs, this value yielded a false-merge rate below 1 % 1\% while capturing over 90 % 90\% of cross-dataset duplicates.

